From: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath12k: free TX status on datapath setup failure

Release and clear already allocated TX status buffers when a later ring
allocation or RX setup fails. The core caller does not deinitialize DP
after unsuccessful setup, so these buffers otherwise lose their owner.
The 512 MiB profile can retain up to 2 MiB per failed device setup.

Signed-off-by: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/dp.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/dp.c
@@ -1573,9 +1573,6 @@ static int ath12k_dp_setup(struct ath12k
 		dp->tx_ring[i].tx_status = kmalloc(size, GFP_KERNEL);
 		if (!dp->tx_ring[i].tx_status) {
 			ret = -ENOMEM;
-			/* FIXME: The allocated tx status is not freed
-			 * properly here
-			 */
 			goto fail_cmn_reoq_cleanup;
 		}
 	}
@@ -1595,6 +1592,11 @@ fail_dp_rx_free:
 	ath12k_dp_rx_free(ab);
 
 fail_cmn_reoq_cleanup:
+	for (i = 0; i < ab->hw_params->max_tx_ring; i++) {
+		kfree(dp->tx_ring[i].tx_status);
+		dp->tx_ring[i].tx_status = NULL;
+	}
+
 	ath12k_dp_reoq_lut_addr_reset(dp);
 	ath12k_dp_reoq_lut_cleanup(ab);
 
